title: Enterococcus
---

# Enterococcus

- **Enterococcus** - Lancefield group D species along w/ S. bovis:
  - **Common sites** - part of <u>normal gut flora</u>, often causing opportunistic infections (e.g. biliary sepsis in cholangitis)
  - **Medically important species:**
    - E. faecalis (less ABx resistance)
    - E. faecium
  - **Clinical associations:**
    - Catheter associated UTI
    - Intra-abdominal/ biliary infections
    - Line sepsis
    - Endocarditis
  - **ABx resistance** - all anterococcus are resistant to cephalosporin
    - <u>E. faecalis</u> - resistant to cephalosporin, but may still be Sn to other beta-lactams
    - <u>E. faecium</u> - typically Sn to big-gun drugs like vancomycin, but emerging resistance to vancomycin (Vancomycin resistant enterococcus \[VRE\]) requiring treatment w/ daptomycin, linezolid, tigecycline
